# Copy this file to .fkst/env (gitignored):
#
#   cp .fkst/env.example .fkst/env
#
# Only the BIN= line is read from it. scripts/bin_bootstrap.sh greps this file for
# `^BIN=` and ignores every other line, so no other setting placed here has any
# effect.

# Path to the fkst-framework binary built from the fkst-substrate repo.
# Typically the sibling checkout: <parent>/fkst-substrate/target/debug/fkst-framework
# Resolution order is: $BIN, then this line, then PATH, then ../fkst-substrate,
# and finally a build of the revision pinned in .fkst/substrate-ref.
BIN=/path/to/fkst-substrate/target/debug/fkst-framework

# --- Everything else is an environment variable, not a line in this file ---
#
# Export FKST_NO_AUTOBUILD=1 to skip the freshness build before test and run.
# scripts/run.sh defaults FKST_RUNTIME_ROOT and FKST_DURABLE_ROOT to
# .fkst/run/runtime and .fkst/run/durable when they are unset.
#
# The FKST_GITHUB_* and FKST_DEVLOOP_* variables are host posture, and this
# repository no longer supplies them. A deployment declares them in
# fkst-deployments and fkst-ops derives the supervise environment from that
# declaration. Setting them here would do nothing twice over: this file is not
# sourced, and scripts/run.sh unsets them anyway -- `run` clears
# FKST_GITHUB_WRITE so a single department run cannot mutate GitHub, and the
# test path clears the whole hermetic set so tests cannot read host posture.
